# term (roadmap os-server.md P12): /dev/com2, with a modem at the far end
# (the runner's HayesPeer; the image built with COM2 the modem and the log
# on COM3): what is typed goes out, the echo and the answers come back
# through IRQ3; term waits in poll for the terminal and the line. MAME's AT
# has no COM3 for the log, and DOSBox-X no drive C.
program: sh
modem: hayes
install: C /BIN/TERM z-term.rx
keys: term\n{wait 10}AT\n{wait 50}ati\n{wait 50}atz\n{wait 50}{esc}
timeout: 60
emulators: bochs
---
rx286, test build
/a$ term
Terminal on COM2 at 9600 baud; Esc ends.
AT
OK
ati
rx286 test modem
OK
atz
ERROR
/a$
